  "term": "muscae volitantes",
  "definition": "Muscae volitantes are floating visual appearances seen within the eye, caused by small particles in the vitreous humor. They may look like bright threads, bead-like strings, dots, or tiny rings, and commonly seem to drift downward across the visual field.",
